    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. So if the relative intensities of those overtones change, the color of the sound changes too. I've heard people talk about \"ghost notes\" or certain frequencies that sound a bit more \"mysterious\" or \"hidden\" than others in woodwinds. Is there a mathematical reason why some overtones might feel slightly detached or less prominent than the fundamental?",
