      "content": "Indeed, inharmonic relationships and amplitude fractions can create a sense of \"trickling\" or \"scurrying\" noises, often referred to as \"ambient\" or \"coloratura\" textures. In formal acoustics, these non-integer overtones are sometimes categorized as \"non-rational\" or \"inharmonic\" harmonics, distinct from the more commonly studied integer multiples (1:1, 2:1, 3:2, etc.). Researchers and musicians use various mathematical and psychoacoustic frameworks to describe and analyze these subtle, inharmonic phenomena that add richness and expressiveness to the sound.",
